Equal sharing means dividing the total cost by the number of people. A billion is \(1000\) million, so \(20\) billion is \(20{,}000\) million. Dividing both numbers by one million simplifies the calculation:
\[
\frac{20{,}000{,}000{,}000}{250{,}000{,}000}
=\frac{20{,}000}{250}
=\frac{2000}{25}
=80.
\]
Each person’s share is \(\boxed{\$80}\), choice \(\boxed{\text{C}}\).
